From 28812444bc918507c17becad55d41d84e6277f62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:30:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer, windowing/gbm: "Picture in step with its sound",
 a setting in place of a key of advancedsettings.xml

The frames chosen for the measured time of their flips were turned off by
<measuredlatency> under <video> in advancedsettings.xml. They are now a
setting of their own, on by default, in Settings > Player > Videos >
Playback, right after "Sync playback to display", at the advanced level:
"Picture in step with its sound". The key of advancedsettings.xml goes
(it was never published): one way to turn it off.

- Its help says, in plain words, what it corrects (the picture left a
  refresh before its sound), that which frames are seen and for how long
  does not change, that each display mode is measured the first time while
  a video plays, where it works (a refresh rate that is a whole multiple of
  the frame rate), and that an "Audio offset" set to make up for it goes
  back to 0. English first; Spanish (es_es, es_ar, es_mx) through Estuary,
  with the name of that setting as Kodi shows it in each.
- A change of the setting is taken where a new measurement is: at the next
  video or seek, never in the middle of what plays.
- Off, nothing is taken (CLatencyMemory::Taken()): the frames are chosen by
  Kodi's latency as they were. What was measured stays kept, and is taken
  again when the setting is on, for the same GPU, driver and build.
- The lines of kodi.log name the setting.
